# Two Nafs Asps deal combat damage to Bot2: each trigger makes its own "loses 1 life at the beginning of their next draw
# step unless they pay {1} before that draw step" (the 2004-10-04 ruling: hit twice, pay or lose twice). Bot2, the
# player dealt damage and not the Asps' controller, pays {1} once in their upkeep - a special action (CR 116.2c), its one
# Mox spent and nothing left in the pool - so of the two only one triggers at their draw step: 20 - 2 - 1 = 17 (CR 603.7).
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Nafs Asp
Nafs Asp
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Nafs Asp.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Nafs Asp.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Nafs Asp#1; Nafs Asp#2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 18
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot2.Nafs Asp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
? Bot2.Mana =
? Bot2.Life = 18
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Tapped = true
